# Documentation

The repository is the source of truth. Anything only in a chat is undocumented.

When you change... update:

| Change | Update |
|---|---|
| Architecture | `docs/02-architecture/*` + ADR in `docs/12-decisions/` |
| Database schema | `docs/03-database/schema.md` (+ `erd.md`, `indexes.md`) |
| API | `docs/07-api/*` |
| Permissions | `docs/04-security/authorization.md` |
| Feature / workflow | `docs/05-features/<feature>.md` (use the template in `docs/05-features/README.md`) |
| Deployment / ops | `docs/09-devops/*`, `docs/11-runbooks/*` |
| Env variables | `.env.example` + `docs/09-devops/environment.md` |
| New dependency | `docs/02-architecture/dependencies.md` |
| User-visible behaviour | `CHANGELOG.md` (Added/Changed/Fixed/Security/Deprecated/Removed) |

After any significant feature update `docs/00-overview/current-state.md`,
`implementation-status.md` and `known-issues.md`.

- Never describe planned features as implemented.
- Use glossary terms (`docs/00-overview/glossary.md`): Tenant, Business Type, Engine, Module, Workspace...
- ADR format: Title, Status, Date, Context, Decision, Alternatives, Consequences.
- Finish tasks with a report: what changed, files, DB changes, tests run, docs updated, risks, follow-ups.
